  "prefLabel": "Saf-C 1401.09 Bumper boats",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Saf-C 1401.09 “Bumper boats” means boats of the same configuration, that are designed to collide with other bumper boats and are located in an enclosed body of water, such as a pool.\n\nSource. #4321, eff 10-6-87; ss by #4531, eff 1-1-89; ss by #5940, INTERIM, eff 1-1-95; ss by #5952, eff 1-24-95, EXPIRED: 1-24-03\n\nNew. #7833, INTERIM, eff 2-22-03, EXPIRED: 8-21-03\n\nNew. #8045, eff 2-20-04; ss by #10131, eff 5-18-12; EXPIRED: 5-18-22\n\nNew. #13535, INTERIM, 1-25-23; ss by #13666, eff 6-20-23; ss by #14139, eff 11-28-24, EXPIRES: 11-28-34 (formerly Saf-C 1401.05) (see Revision Note #3 at chapter heading for Saf-C 1400)",
